From 32d69a37311f58a057092dc174e1869706df599f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:16:57 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] PLACEHOLDER: ir3: don't use MGEN.B for nir_op_bfm on a3xx

23007dcb077 ("ir3: Add support for nir_op_bfm (ir3's MGEN)") set
has_bfm for every generation. On A306 (FD307) MGEN.B does not write
the mask at all: a sweep of 48 bits/offset combinations through
`((1u << bits) - 1u) << offset` (which nir_opt_algebraic turns into
bfm and ir3 into `mgen.b`) returned 0 for every case whose expected
mask is nonzero, and the first draw returned stale register contents
(0x3f7fe1a7). Only the cases whose mask is 0 anyway matched.

That makes the four piglit
spec@mesa_shader_integer_functions@execution@built-in-functions
{fs,vs}-bitfield{Extract,Insert} tests fail, and fs-bitfieldInsert
hangs the GPU: the only branch that depends on the mask was compiled
as uniform, and with per-fibre garbage it diverges without
reconverging. Writing a constant into the destination before the
mgen.b, or adding (jp) to the branch target, both make the hang go
away (the results stay wrong). Reverting 23007dcb077 fixes all four
tests. Mesa's a306 nightly piglit jobs have shown the same failures
and hangcheck since 2026-09-23.

a5xx, a6xx and a7xx pass the same tests with MGEN.B in CI, so only
a3xx is gated. a4xx has no CI and was not tested; its 2021
expectation files list none of the bitcount/bitfieldReverse failures
that a306 has for the related cat2 bit ops, so it is left as it was.

With this change on A306: the 60 mesa_shader_integer_functions tests
give 56 Pass + 4 ExpectedFail with no hangcheck, and the full
quick_shader profile differs from the pre-23007dcb077 baseline only in
those four tests going from Fail to Pass. FD420/FD530/FD630 codegen
for the affected shaders is byte-identical before and after.

Fixes: 23007dcb077 ("ir3: Add support for nir_op_bfm (ir3's MGEN).")

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c
index 5bb326fbb52..8d12b550ae7 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c
@@ -158,7 +158,6 @@ static const nir_shader_compiler_options ir3_base_options = {
    .lower_pack_split = true,
    .lower_pack_64_4x16 = true,
    .lower_to_scalar = true,
-   .has_bfm = true,
    .has_find_msb_rev = true,
    .has_imul24 = true,
    .has_umul24 = true,
@@ -384,6 +383,12 @@ ir3_compiler_create(struct fd_device *dev, const struct fd_dev_id *dev_id,
    /* Set up nir shader compiler options, using device-specific overrides of our base settings. */
    compiler->nir_options = ir3_base_options;
    compiler->nir_options.has_iadd3 = dev_info->props.has_sad;
+   /* MGEN.B doesn't produce usable results on a3xx (A306: wrong
+    * bitfieldInsert/bitfieldExtract results, and a GPU hang when a branch
+    * depends on them), so keep bfm open-coded there.  a5xx and later are
+    * known to be fine; a4xx is untested.
+    */
+   compiler->nir_options.has_bfm = compiler->gen >= 4;
 
    if (compiler->gen >= 6) {
       compiler->nir_options.force_indirect_unrolling = nir_var_all,
